    },
    {
      title: "Read-only admin cost/margin dashboard (shipped, /admin)",
      description:
        "Owner-only (role=ADMIN gate) view of every Build row: real cost (from metered token usage), credits charged, derived gross margin $ and %, recent-build table with status. Unit economics is Kodely's #1 existential risk per the research — this gives visibility from day one instead of flying blind. No promotion path to ADMIN role exists yet (deliberately out of scope for this wave).",
    },
    {
      title: "Stripe credit top-ups wired, INERT until real keys are set (shipped, gated)",
      description:
        "Full money-path: fixed server-side credit packs ($9/500, $40/2500, $90/6000 — client only ever sends a pack id, never an amount), Stripe Checkout session creation, and a signature-verified webhook that grants credits ONLY on confirmed payment (never the client-side success redirect) with a StripeEvent claim-row guarding against double-grant on webhook retries. Currently returns a clean 503 'Billing isn't set up yet' everywhere — needs real STRIPE_SECRET_KEY + STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET before it does anything. OWNER ACTION: create a Stripe account/keys when ready to accept real payment.",
    },
    {
      title: "⚠️ BLOCKER: *.kodely.site nginx never wired to the app — publish URLs don't resolve",
      description:
        "Found + diagnosed 2026-08-17: the Kodely VM's internal nginx (/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/kodely) still routes kodely.site and *.kodely.site to a leftover static placeholder directory from initial provisioning (root /var/www/kodely-site-router), never updated to proxy into the Next.js app like the kodely.me block does. Effect: Publish succeeds and returns a URL, but visiting it shows a generic Cloudflare/nginx error page instead of the real site — the one-click-deploy feature is currently broken end-to-end on the serving side. FIX IS READY, blocked only on sudo (harness classifier gates system-config edits from chat regardless of approval): swap that block's `root ...; index ...;` for the same `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;` block already used by kodely.me. One-line copy-paste fix, given to the user 2026-08-17, not yet confirmed applied.",
    },
  ];

  let pos = existingCards.length > 0 ? Math.max(...existingCards.map((c) => c.position)) + 1 : 0;
  for (const c of newCards) {
    if (has(c.title)) continue;
    await db.card.create({ data: { boardId: BOARD, columnId: shipped.id, title: c.title, description: c.description, position: pos++ } });
    console.log("added card:", c.title);
  }

  await db.$disconnect();
}

