Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The overarching project is "Kodely" — an AI website builder SaaS venture under the user's Nxeon hub, running on a dedicated Proxmox-hosted VM (10.20.0.30, internal IP, no public IP) accessible via `ssh 10.20.0.30` (root, key-based). Prod is `kodely.me` (`/opt/kodely`, systemd `kodely.service` :3000), staging is `staging.kodely.me` (`/opt/kodely-staging`, `kodely-staging.service` :3001), and the actual dev/build workspace with full git history is `/home/kodely/kodely-dev` on that VM (connected to `origin` = `github.com:santino1233/kodely.git`; git operations must run as the `kodely` user via `sudo -u kodely`, not root, since the deploy key lives at `/home/kodely/.ssh/kodely_github`). Deploy = `/home/kodely/deploy.sh [prod|staging]` (fetch+reset origin/main → npm ci → build → restart → healthcheck).

   Within this summarized window, the user's explicit requests in chronological order were:
   - Continue the SEO content backlog (batches 3 and 4 shipped, bringing total to 56/251 live blog posts).
   - "I dont like this at all on the homepage. looks terrible. lets do something else entirely" (re: the ShowcaseCarousel component) — with an attached screenshot showing a row of small browser-chip cards.
   - "is there a way we can have kodely run off of my claude subscription. I did this before with nxeon with matrix app. there has to be a way here" — followed by ~6 more messages pushing on this from different angles ("can i start using it right away", "what if we wire in claude on ssh and send commands through there", "what if we did it on localhost?", "kodely is for my to make websites for my clients", "I swear it on the quran, im using this for my own personal use", "lets use claude subscription, i need to for testing").
   - Reported a real cost scare: "we are not live now and i just tried to make a website and it drained $2.45 in api credits" and later "so something from kodely used the api key costing this much credits" and "how can i use claude subscription for testing" and "and avoid api key credits".
   - "is there a way to constantly build kodely skills from the website makes automatically in the background" (asking about automating free test-site seeding).
   - "we shouldnt be using api credits to build kodely, thats why i have claude max" (clarification request about what actually costs API money).
   - "can i build sites for kodely from this chat then for testing purposes" then "and avoid api key credits" (led to building `scripts/seed-test-sites.ts`).
   - Major new feature request (verbatim): "I would like to change the beginning section of the Codely website. I really like the feel of the Google Gemini chat UI with the nice glow illuminating around the chat. I wanna make this website as engaging as possible, and I wanna prompt people to type in a prompt right from the beginning to get them engaged on the website. Obviously, if they are not logged in, as soon as they hit enter on the prompt, then they will be prompted to sign up or log in. However, I want that prompt that they originally typed in to carry through their login or sign up process and then finally get processed once they are logged in. Obviously, keep the color scheme the same with the warm pink gradient that we have throughout the entire website, but I wanna give it a liquid glass iOS twenty six feel."
   - Most recent (the active task): "As soon as I get onto the website, there is that illuminating glow around the chat box, which is very which is very vibrant, and I think it's a little too opaque. I want it to be more of an accent glow. Within a few seconds of loading the website, the glow immediately disappears. So it needs to be static and pulsating in the background behind the prompt chat box."

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Prisma + PostgreSQL, Tailwind CSS v4 (CSS-first, no config file), framer-motion for animation.
   - Anthropic Claude Sonnet 5 for codegen via `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, metered credit billing (`lib/credits.ts`, `lib/models.ts` EFFORT/MODEL_RATES), self-repair loop (max 2 attempts), AbortController tied to SSE stream cancellation so client disconnects don't get charged.
   - "Kodely Luxe" locked design system: near-monochrome base, brand gradient (coral→magenta→purple, `var(--brand-gradient)`) spent deliberately not as a wash, calm physics-eased motion, "one real hero object" rule (not many small skeleton-style elements), never a color-cycling shimmer (only rejected in earlier project history).
   - Anthropic authentication surfaces researched in depth: raw Messages API (3 methods only: API key, Workload Identity Federation, iOS/macOS App Attest — no subscription path for third parties); Claude Agent SDK (does support subscription OAuth via `claude setup-token`, works headlessly, but Anthropic's docs explicitly require prior written approval for third-party product embedding: "Unless previously approved, Anthropic does not allow third party developers to offer claude.ai login or rate limits for their products, including agents built on the Claude Agent SDK.").
   - `buildSite()` (`lib/build-site.ts`) — a pure local `vite build` compile step against a pre-installed foundation dependency tree, NO Anthropic API call — key insight enabling free test-site seeding.
   - sessionStorage-based state carry-through across auth flow (`kodely:pending_prompt` key).
   - Playwright (via `/opt/nxeon/node_modules/playwright`, scripts must run from within `/opt/nxeon` for module resolution) for visual verification — screenshots, computed-style inspection, real end-to-end auth flow testing.
   - CSS `color-mix()` for tinted borders; `backdrop-blur` + `backdrop-saturate` for glassmorphism; multi-layer absolutely-positioned blurred gradient blobs for ambient glow effects.
   - Empirical debugging methodology: when investigating a reported animation/visual bug, check actual computed styles over time via Playwright rather than guessing from code review alone.

